 "rule_doc": "M1 (07:30 gap model) vs THE SIMPLE HISTORY LINE, on the SAME unseen days (DESK_REVIEW 21 Nov 16:00 point 3). Code only, no network.\nTHE LINE (rule): NQ futures move from India's close (15:30 IST) to 07:30 IST next morning - M1's own window. |move| >= 1% -> call the gap's\nsign = the move's sign; smaller -> no call. (The desk's quoted '81% (186 cases)' is the gap study's NQ 14:30 -> 09:00 IST window, which ends\nafter the 07:15 brief; it is shown for reference on the same days.)\nM1 = the walk-forward probabilities of the saved 07:30 models (intraday: with the NQ / ES / SOX night moves; daily: S&P / Nasdaq cash), each\nunseen year scored by a model trained only on earlier years. Unseen days = 2025 and 2026 (the NQ 60m history starts Jul 2024).\nPASS (M1 beats the line), all of:\n  (1) MATCHED COVERAGE: per year M1 calls only its k most confident days, k = the line's calls that year; pooled hit rate beats the line's\n      with a one-sided two-proportion p < 0.025;\n  (2) BOTH SIDES: at matched coverage M1's GAP-UP calls and GAP-DOWN calls each hit more often than the line's up / down calls;\n  (3) more than half the years: M1's matched-coverage hit rate beats the line's in each year (2 of 2);\n  (4) Brier on the line's call days: M1's p beats the line's p (= the line's hit rate on the training years).\nAlso shown: head-to-head on the line's call days, M1 on the days the line makes no call, and a long-history proxy (Nasdaq Composite cash\nnight move >= 1% vs the daily M1, unseen years 2015-2026).\nRun (venv): nice -n 15 /home/globalbot/venvs/gir-models/bin/python m1_vs_line.py  -> appends to models_M1.md, writes m1_vs_line.json",
